cilities and possible research/thesis projects using the samples were discussed. Agreements at university or faculty level were mentioned as options; no research agreement or test programme was finalised.\nImplementation issues: University participants highlighted the importance of informing designers before technical specifications restrict material choices. Certification and market-entry requirements need checking. A presenter stated that European-sourced components have certificates; this does not establish compliance or certification of the final mixture or intended application.\nFollow-up: The presenter indicated an intention to assemble and send materials next week, 19–25 October, then coordinate interested researchers and themes. No exact delivery date, test date, cost or responsible technical contact was agreed.\nSource: User-provided Polish meeting transcript; some names, product terms and speaker identities remain uncertain.",
